# VulnHunter repository authority

Read `AGENTS.md` in full before changing the repository. It is the binding operating manual.

For browser/UI work, follow the exact additional read order in `vulnhunter/web/AGENTS.md`.

Permanent rules:

- authorised private and public targets are supported product classes;
- a public URL is never permission;
- public execution must follow `docs/product/PUBLIC_TARGET_ASSESSMENT.md` and preserve explicit authorization, target class, worker capability, DNS/address containment and Host/TLS identity;
- never globally relax scope checks or delete private-worker restrictions to make public scanning work;
- queued/running work must follow `docs/product/LIVE_EXECUTION_ACTIVITY.md` and expose persisted operational activity, not fake progress;
- Source Hunt follows `docs/product/SOURCE_HUNT.md`, including preflight and truthful permitted-path/snapshot semantics;
- browser UI follows the locked `docs/design/` authority chain and remains conversation/task-first;
- never expose hidden chain-of-thought/private model reasoning;
- models never grant authorization, execution, verification, review, merge, release or publication authority;
- `docs/intelligence/CURRENT_STATE.md` owns implementation truth;
- `docs/intelligence/ROADMAP.md` owns current dependency order;
- historical milestone/total-programme/future-plan files do not override current authorities.

If the requested task conflicts with a binding boundary, stop and report the exact conflict rather than weakening the product.
